1. Scope and definitions

This License applies to original GLGMesh code and accompanying documentation
expressly distributed under this License (the "Software"), including copies,
modifications and portions of that code. The copyright holders grant only
rights they own or are authorized to grant. All other rights are reserved.

"Third-Party Materials" means software, libraries, dependencies, model code,
model weights, datasets and other materials supplied by other rights holders,
including third-party portions of modified files. Third-Party Materials are
not relicensed by this License and remain subject to their individual terms.

"Generated Assets" means meshes, textures, renders, animations and other
creative assets that you create or process using the Software. Generated
Assets do not include the Software, model weights or other software merely
copied or embedded in an output. Bundled showcase media, example artwork and
other pre-existing assets are not granted a new license by this definition.

"Commercial Software Use" means incorporating, embedding, integrating,
distributing, selling, licensing or otherwise using the Software or any
portion of its code as part of a software product or service operated for
commercial advantage or monetary compensation. This includes paid or
commercially supported applications, plugins, SDKs, APIs, hosted services,
SaaS, commercially operated internal software integrations, and services
that expose GLGMesh functionality to third parties. Providing free access
does not exempt an otherwise commercial software product or service.
The asset-creation exception in Section 4 takes precedence over this
definition.

