3. Separate license for commercial software

This License does not authorize Commercial Software Use. Before undertaking
Commercial Software Use, you must obtain a separate written commercial
license from Edgechasers. Contact:

    Edgechasers
    glgmesh@edgechasers.com

Attribution, payment for another product, or simply sending a license request
does not grant commercial software rights. The separate agreement must
expressly authorize the intended use. Unless that agreement expressly varies
the GLGMesh attribution terms, Section 5 continues to apply. A commercial
license from Edgechasers cannot waive obligations owed to third-party rights
holders.

4. Generated Assets and commercial asset creation

You may use, reproduce, modify, display, perform, distribute, sell and
otherwise exploit Generated Assets for any purpose, including commercial
purposes, subject to the attribution in Section 5 and applicable third-party
rights and licenses in Section 6. No separate GLGMesh commercial license or
royalty is required merely because an asset is used commercially.

You may run GLGMesh as an asset-production tool to create assets for yourself,
your organization or clients, including paid client work and batch processing.
Selling those assets, or including them in paid games, films, applications,
asset packs or other products, does not constitute Commercial Software Use
when the product contains the assets rather than GLGMesh code or access to
GLGMesh functionality. This exception does not authorize a commercial
software integration or a hosted generation service covered by Section 3.

The GLGMesh copyright holders claim no ownership of your Generated Assets
merely because GLGMesh was used to create them. To the extent they hold any
rights in such assets solely through GLGMesh's generation or processing,
they grant permission to exercise those rights on the terms of this section.
No ownership, copyrightability or third-party clearance is guaranteed.

5. Required attribution

The required attribution is the following exact text:

    powered by GLGMesh

For code use, provide this credit clearly and legibly in the product or
service interface, an accessible About or Credits page, or its primary
user-facing documentation. For a library, SDK, command-line tool or use
without a conventional interface, include it in the primary documentation
or accompanying notice. Include it with distributed source code as well.
For wholly private code use, retain it in the project's documentation or
internal notices; no public disclosure of private work is required.

For Generated Assets, retain the credit in asset metadata or accompanying
records. Whenever you distribute, publish, display or use assets in a
product, also provide the credit in a reasonably accessible location, such
as the asset listing or description, accompanying README or attribution
file, or the product's credits, About page or documentation. One clearly
applicable credit may cover multiple GLGMesh assets in the same work or
collection. A visual watermark on the asset itself is not required.

When supplying Generated Assets to another person, include this attribution
requirement and require that the credit be preserved in subsequent uses and
redistributions, including modified versions. Do not remove or conceal
existing GLGMesh attribution in a manner that defeats these requirements.

These requirements apply to all purposes for which GLGMesh code is used,
including purposes not specifically listed above, and to the asset permission
in Section 4. They do not apply to independently obtained Third-Party
Materials merely because GLGMesh also uses those materials.

You may use the GLGMesh name solely as needed to provide this attribution
and accurately identify the Software. No endorsement, sponsorship or other
trademark permission is implied.

